      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We granted certiorari."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8efa05321ad41a05288b326714ba62acb7f259b789a5e70335653034f69d9ad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8efa05321ad4-0000-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A federal court's power to grant habeas relief is restricted under the Antiterrorism and Effective Death Penalty Act of 1996 (AEDPA), which provides that the writ may issue \u201conly on the ground that [the prisoner] is in custody in violation of the Constitution or laws or treaties of the United States.\u201d 28 U. S. C. \u00a7 2254(a)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8efa05321ad41a05288b326714ba62acb7f259b789a5e70335653034f69d9ad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8efa05321ad4-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court entered an order directing the State to transport Twyford to a medical facility, concluding that doing so would aid its adjudication of his habeas petition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8efa05321ad41a05288b326714ba62acb7f259b789a5e70335653034f69d9ad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8efa05321ad4-0001-0000",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "majority",
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The District Court thus erred in ordering Twyford's transfer to gather evidence he had never demonstrated would be admissible."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-21-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8efa05321ad41a05288b326714ba62acb7f259b789a5e70335653034f69d9ad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8efa05321ad4-0002-0000",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For these reasons, I would not reach the merits of the questions presented by petitioner. I respectfully dissent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-511",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8efa05321ad41a05288b326714ba62acb7f259b789a5e70335653034f69d9ad2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8efa05321ad4-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": "dissent",
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court granted review to decide whether and under what circumstances a federal district court may order a State to transport a prisoner to a hospital for testing."
    }
  ],
